-- Advance Database Management System | Mid 1 | medium | TestId 440009351502015 | theory
INSERT INTO public."TestsData" ("TestId", "Questions", "Options", "Answers")
VALUES (440009351502015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Advance Database Management System requires the behaviour described by one set of attributes determines the value of another set in a relation. Explain how Introduction to functional dependency applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Advance Database Management System requires the behaviour described by tables are reorganized to reduce redundancy and modification anomalies according to dependency rules. Explain how Introduction to normalization applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Advance Database Management System requires the behaviour described by the course topic concerned with Transaction concept. Explain how Transaction concept applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Advance Database Management System requires the behaviour described by one set of attributes determines the value of another set in a relation. Explain how key terms for functional dependency applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A functional dependency X→Y means each value of attribute set X determines a single value of Y in every valid row. Dependencies help identify keys, redundancy and suitable decompositions.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to key terms for functional dependency; rules of functional dependency; types of functional dependency: Multivalued dependency; trivial functional dependency. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Normalization applies dependency-based rules to reduce redundancy and insertion, update and deletion anomalies. 1NF removes repeating groups, 2NF removes partial dependency on a candidate key, and 3NF/BCNF impose stronger dependency conditions.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Normal Form: First Normal Form (1NF); Second Normal Form(2NF); Third Normal Form(3NF); Boyce Codd Normal Form(BCNF). State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Concurrency control coordinates transactions that overlap in time. Locking controls access to data; correctness depends on lock compatibility, ordering and release, while poor locking can cause waiting or deadlocks.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to ACID property; basics of Concurrency; method of Concurrency control: Locking method; Timestamp method. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** A functional dependency X→Y means each value of attribute set X determines a single value of Y in every valid row. Dependencies help identify keys, redundancy and suitable decompositions.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Introduction to functional dependency; rules of functional dependency; types of functional dependency: Multivalued dependency; trivial functional dependency. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Advance Database Management System task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

