VALUES (440009351506015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamentals Of IOT With Python requires the behaviour described by physical devices use sensing, processing and communication to share data and support actions. Explain how Defining IoT applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamentals Of IOT With Python requires the behaviour described by devices exchange information or trigger actions with limited direct human involvement. Explain how Machine to Machine applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamentals Of IOT With Python requires the behaviour described by the course topic concerned with Home automation. Explain how Home automation applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Fundamentals Of IOT With Python requires the behaviour described by physical devices use sensing, processing and communication to share data and support actions. Explain how Characteristics of IoT applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IoT connects physical devices, sensors and actuators through processing and communication. Security, reliability, connectivity and power constraints are central.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Characteristics of IoT; Physical design of Iot; Logical design of IoT; Functional blocks of IoT. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Machine-to-machine communication allows devices or systems to exchange data and coordinate actions automatically; IoT often includes a broader connected application ecosystem.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Difference between IoT and M2M; Software define Network; IoT & M2M. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IoT connects physical devices, sensors and actuators through processing and communication. Security, reliability, connectivity and power constraints are central.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Industry applications; Environment applications; Other IoT applications; Challenges in IoT. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** IoT connects physical devices, sensors and actuators through processing and communication. Security, reliability, connectivity and power constraints are central.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Defining IoT; Physical design of Iot; Logical design of IoT; Functional blocks of IoT. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Fundamentals Of IOT With Python task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

