VALUES (440009351501015, ARRAY['"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mobile Computing requires the behaviour described by the course topic concerned with History. Explain how History applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mobile Computing requires the behaviour described by the course topic concerned with TCP/IP Protocol suit. Explain how TCP/IP Protocol suit applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mobile Computing requires the behaviour described by a 2G cellular standard defines radio access, identifiers, mobility and subscriber authentication. Explain how GSM :- call routing Architecture applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb, '"[8 marks] A practical problem in Mobile Computing requires the behaviour described by the course topic concerned with Types. Explain how Types applies, outline the steps and justify the result."'::jsonb]::jsonb[], ARRAY[]::jsonb[], ARRAY['"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** History appears in “What is Mobile Computing”. Define its role, explain the main steps/components as taught, relate it to Types, Benefits, Application, Evolution, give an example from the course, and note a validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to Types; Benefits; Application; Evolution. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Mobile Computing task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** TCP/IP Protocol suit appears in “Wireless Transmission Fundamentals”. Define its role, explain the main steps/components as taught, relate it to OSI Reference Model, Modulation, Modulation Techniques FDMA/TDMA/CDMA, WAP Architecture, give an example from the course, and note a validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to OSI Reference Model; Modulation; Modulation Techniques FDMA/TDMA/CDMA; WAP Architecture. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Mobile Computing task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** GSM is a 2G cellular system with radio access, subscriber identities, authentication, network elements and handover procedures.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to PLMN interface; addresses and identifiers; network aspects; frequency allocation. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Mobile Computing task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb, '"Model answer (8 marks)\n\n**Meaning and purpose (2 marks):** Types appears in “What is Mobile Computing”. Define its role, explain the main steps/components as taught, relate it to History, Benefits, Application, Evolution, give an example from the course, and note a validation check or limitation.\n\n**Principles/steps (3 marks):** Explain the concept in logical order and relate it to History; Benefits; Application; Evolution. State applicable rules, components, assumptions or formulas.\n\n**Application/example (2 marks):** Apply it to a specific Mobile Computing task. State the objective, method and expected outcome.\n\n**Verification/conclusion (1 mark):** Check the result against the objective, note a limitation or error source, and justify the choice.\n\nMarking guide: meaning 2; principles/steps 3; application 2; verification 1."'::jsonb]::jsonb[]);

